\par\par \b \uc2 Sing dollar at one-month high, spurred by yen, yuan  \b0\par\par\uc2 308 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 M\u228\'00\'E4rz 2006\par 03:30\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, March 1 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar hit its highest level in a month on Wednesday, lifted by a rising Japanese yen and Chinese yuan, but operators were wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rein the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in.  \par \par \uc2 The Sing dollar <SGD=> hit 1.6198 per U.S. dollar in early deals, its strongest level since the end of January, taking its gain to more than one percent in less than two weeks. It later steadied around 1.6205/15.  \par \par \uc2 Traders suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  on Tuesday to slow down the Sing dollar's rise.  \par \par \uc2 "MAS has been tempering the pace of appreciation. But I expect both the yuan and yen to appreciate strongly over the next 10 to 15 days and these will pull the Sing dollar with them," one Singapore-based trader said.  \par \par \uc2 The yen <JPY=> was quoted around 115.95 a dollar. It has risen more than 2.5 percent in a week on expectations of a near-term end to Japan's ultra-easy monetary policy.  \par \par \uc2 The Chinese yuan has risen this week to its highest level since its revaluation last July.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts estimated that the Sing dollar's rise this year had taken it to the top end of the MAS's policy band.  \par \par \uc2 The MAS conducts monetary policy by managing the Singapore dollar within an undisclosed band based on a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 JPMorgan strategist Claudio Piron said in a note the Sing dollar was particularly susceptible to any decline in the yen.  \par \par \uc2 But traders were bullish. "I don't think it's too expensive. We do have a reasonable chance to go towards 1.6120," one said.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SINGAPORE-DOLLAR|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060301e2310004p\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
