\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Falls, Bonds Stabilize After Losses  \b0\par\par\uc2 526 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 28 Februar 2006\par 08:03\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar fell Tuesday due to pent-up corporate buying of the U.S. dollar to meet month-end payments and on talk of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Government bonds stabilized after two days of losses as corporate buyers returned to seek bargains, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0615 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6241, up from S$1.6230 in late New York trade Monday. It traded at S$1.6244 in late Asian trade Friday.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar moved between S$1.6215 and S$1.6259 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. unit pulled up from a morning low of S$1.6232 to S$1.6255 on talk that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore may have checked the Singapore's unit rise, a trader at a local bank said.  \par \par \uc2 Later, importers came back into the market to buy the greenback to meet corporate payments, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Against the yen, the U.S. unit rose to a session high of Y116.49 on the EBS before slipping to Y116.32, compared to Y116.20 at the New York close.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the Singapore dollar's recent gains were due to strength in the yen, but room for more gains was limited.  \par \par \uc2 Sean Callow, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Westpac Bank, said he favors long U.S. dollar positions against the Singapore dollar because the trade-weighted Singapore dollar has, he believes, reached the top of \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's undisclosed target band.  \par \par \uc2 "Hence we would not be in the least surprised if Tuesday's market anecdotes of MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on USD/SGD are correct. Short-term, we continue to see risk/reward in favor of long USD/SGD with a S$1.62 handle," Callow said in a note to clients.  \par \par \uc2 He said his outlook should stay intact until the MAS reviews its policy in April. Many in the market expect the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  to push for a steeper appreciation of the local unit to contain inflation.  \par \par \uc2 Bonds consolidated after two days of heavy selling, sparked by last week's 10-year government bond auction, where yields rose sharply.  \par \par \uc2 Both the two- and 10-year bonds closed flat at 2.86% and 3.52% respectively after some weakness in the early session, when the 10-year opened at 3.53%, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The 10-year bond has risen 20 basis points from 3.32% late Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The following are the yields of Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps:  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                       Latest    Previous \par Overnight rate        3.063%    2.938% \par Two-year bond yield   2.86%     2.86% \par 10-year bond yield    3.52%     3.52% \par Two-year swap offer   3.57%     3.56% \par 10-year swap offer    3.76%     3.73% \par 2-10-yr swap spread:  19 BPs    17 BPs \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Ven Ram [ 28-02-06 0703GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060228e22s000ac\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pn