\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dolllar Flat Late; Rumored MAS Action Early  \b0\par\par\uc2 499 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Februar 2006\par 08:34\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar ended a choppy Asian trading session nearly flat against the U.S. dollar Thursday, ahead of the second day of new U.S. Federal Reserve Chairman Ben Bernanke's congressional testimony.  \par \par \uc2 Government bonds weakened slightly in the wake of robust Singapore data, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0645 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6294, almost unchanged from Wednesday's New York close of S$1.6291. It was quoted at S$1.6298 in Asia Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 Early in the session, the U.S. dollar rose to an intraday high of S$1.6320 on interbank-led short-covering spurred by rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  apparently bought the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the S$1.6292-S$1.6295 area via local banks in the morning, prompting interbank players to buy back U.S. dollars, they added.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market participants shrugged off the early morning release of stronger-than-expected \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  data, focusing more on this suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Fourth-quarter gross domestic product grew 8.7% from a year earlier. This beat the 8.2% average growth forecast in a Dow Jones Newswires poll of economists.  \par \par \uc2 Citing stronger domestic and external demand, export-dependent Singapore raised its forecast for gross domestic product growth in 2006 to 4%-6% from 3%-5%.  \par \par \uc2 Some players who had bought back U.S. dollars in the morning took profit in the afternoon, causing the greenback to fall back to the S$1.6290 area.  \par \par \uc2 Late in the session, the U.S. dollar consolidated with a firm tone against the local dollar ahead of the second leg of Bernanke's two-day congressional testimony later in the session.  \par \par \uc2 Bernanke is expected to reiterate the Fed's message that further rate hikes will depend on how U.S. economic data unfold in the coming months. This continuity of former Chairman Alan Greenspan's policy stance could extend the recent U.S. dollar gains versus its rivals.  \par \par \uc2 Yields on Singapore government bonds were higher across the curve, mostly owing to the robust data, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Volume was low ahead of an announcement later in the session of the auction size for the reopening of the 10-year government bond.  \par \par \uc2 The following are the yields of Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps:  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                       Latest    Previous \par Overnight rate        3.0625%   0.6250% \par Two-year bond yield   2.66%     2.64% \par 10-year bond yield    3.29%     3.27% \par Two-year swap offer   3.34%     3.32% \par 10-year swap offer    3.61%     3.58% \par 2-10-yr swap spread:  27 BPs    26 BPs \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4159; ron.harui@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Clarissa Tan [ 16-02-06 0734GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060216e22g000ax\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pi