\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Down Late; Expectation Of Hawkish Bernanke  \b0\par\par\uc2 443 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Februar 2006\par 08:14\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar fell in Asia Monday on expectations that the U.S. Federal Reserve's new chairman might sound a hawkish note at his first congressional testimony later this week.  \par \par \uc2 The government bond yield curve flattened slightly in thin trading ahead of this week's batch of U.S. and Singapore events, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0640 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6303, up from Friday's New York close of S$1.6258. It was quoted at S$1.6282 in Asia Friday.  \par \par \uc2 From early in the session, interbank players bought U.S. dollars for Singapore dollars to cover short positions, lifting the U.S. unit to a morning high of S$1.6299, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The short-covering was spurred by prospects that Fed Chairman Ben Bernanke, at his two-day testimony starting Wednesday, could reaffirm his predecessor Alan Greenspan's upbeat view of the U.S. economy and signal more interest-rate hikes in the coming months.  \par \par \uc2 For the rest of the session, the U.S. dollar consolidated around the psychologically important S$1.6300 resistance level, largely owing to the U.S. unit's resilience against other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Japanese yen.  \par \par \uc2 At 0640 GMT, the U.S. unit was at Y117.92, up slightly from Y117.90 in New York Friday.  \par \par \uc2 One trader said another factor driving the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's rise against the Singapore dollar was expectations that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  could again \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  after it apparently bought U.S. dollars late Friday, when the U.S. unit fell to a one-week low of S$1.6222.  \par \par \uc2 But there were no signs of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by late local trade Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Government bonds hugged tight ranges as players were reluctant to take any large positions ahead of Bernanke's testimony Wednesday and Singapore Prime Minister Lee Hsien Loong's budget presentation Friday, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The following are the yields of Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps:  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                       Latest    Previous \par Overnight rate        2.3750%   2.7500% \par Two-year bond yield   2.66%     2.62% \par 10-year bond yield    3.27%     3.30% \par Two-year swap offer   3.37%     3.37% \par 10-year swap offer    3.60%     3.61% \par 2-10-yr swap spread:  23 BPs    24 BPs \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4159; ron.harui@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Clarissa Tan [ 13-02-06 0714GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060213e22d000b9\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
