\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore dollar near top of band, seen capped  \b0\par\par\uc2 487 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2006\par 10:15\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Feb 1 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar's 2.5 percent rise last month has pushed it to the top of the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy band for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , and markets should be on guard for possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts said on Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar <SGD=> rose to around 1.6207 per U.S. dollar on Wednesday, half a cent away from last week's highs near 1.6170 and defying the U.S. dollar's strength against the yen.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is unwilling to push the Sing dollar higher because it is already close to the top of the band and the strong data will not let it go lower," said UBS's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Ashley Davies.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) conducts monetary policy by managing the Singapore dollar within an undisclosed band against a trade-weighted basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  has maintained a tightening bias by permitting a gradual appreciation of the trade-weighted band since April 2004.  \par \par \uc2 Davies said the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was about 1.8 percent stronger than his estimate of the mid-point of the band. UBS assumes the band is 4 percent wide and the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  allows a modest pace of appreciation for this mid-point, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Some analysts who track the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  based on a 2 percent wide band had said last week the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has breached the top extremity of that band.  \par \par \uc2 Rising asset prices, robust export growth and the strength in economic growth numbers have prompted thinking among economists that the MAS is on the verge of announcing a policy suggesting a faster pace of appreciation for the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The government reported on Wednesday that the island's unemployment rate fell in the fourth quarter to 2.5 percent, the lowest since the second quarter of 2001.  \par \par \uc2 Davies said the Singapore dollar would now be stable, but could gain further in the medium term.  \par \par \uc2 "We still think that SGD will perform well on a medium-term view given the potential for the MAS to adopt a more aggressive tightening bias, should the strong data continue," he said in a note.  \par \par \uc2 Sean Callow, Westpac Bank's strategist, estimated the Singapore dollar was around 2.1 percent above the mid-point of a band he assumes is 4 percent wide.  \par \par \uc2 He said in a note to clients it was possible the MAS would drop the word "modest" from the appreciation bias it has held for nearly 2 years when it reviews policy this April.  \par \par \uc2 "But until then, there can be little doubt that the speed and extent of the SGD rise since mid-Nov will be causing some unease at the MAS."  \par \par \uc2 The gains seemed stretched, Callow said, adding he would not buy the Singapore dollar at these levels.  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SINGAPORE-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060201e221000m2\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
