\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Dn Late After FOMC Signals More Tightening  \b0\par\par\uc2 473 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 1 Februar 2006\par 08:49\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar fell slightly in Asia Wednesday after the Federal Reserve raised U.S. interest rates as expected but signaled the possibility of more monetary tightening.  \par \par \uc2 Prices on government bonds rose in the short end but slipped in the long end, resulting in yield curve steepening, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0710 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6232, up from Tuesday's New York close of S$1.6219. Singapore's markets were closed for Lunar New Year holidays Monday and Tuesday, with the U.S. unit having ended local trade Friday at S$1.6245.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar edged up to an intraday high of S$1.6245 very early in Wednesday's Asian session following the Federal Open Market Committee's statement hinting at more tightening at its next policy-setting meeting on Mar. 28, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 In its statement, the Fed dropped the word "measured," which it had use to describe the previous pace of its rate hikes since it began its tightening in June 2004, and also noted that "some further policy firming may be needed."  \par \par \uc2 Although the U.S. dollar consolidated within a S$1.6210-S$1.6240 range for the rest of Wednesday's Asian session, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  could extend its rebound against the local dollar in the coming sessions, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 "We would prefer not to chase SGD much higher at current prices and see scope for some (downward) retracement (of the Singapore dollar) in the near term," said Westpac Institutional Bank in a research note.  \par \par \uc2 Westpac said the Singapore dollar's current level "is very much in (the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's) \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  territory."  \par \par \uc2 Market speculation believes \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may have contributed to the brevity of the recent U.S. dollar decline below the psychologically important S$1.6200 level, Westpac said.  \par \par \uc2 Yields on short-dated Singapore government bonds fell on domestic investor demand while those on longer-term bonds rose due to higher U.S. Treasury yields Tuesday, leading to a modest steepening of the local bond yield curve, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The following are the yields of Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps:  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                       Latest    Previous \par Overnight rate        3.5625%   3.7500% \par Two-year bond yield   2.66%     2.76% \par 10-year bond yield    3.39%     3.35% \par Two-year swap offer   3.34%     3.32% \par 10-year swap offer    3.69%     3.67% \par 2-10-yr swap spread:  35 BPS    35 BPs \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4159; ron.harui@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Michael Kitchen [ 01-02-06 0749GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060201e221000bm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
