\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Fall from highs,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  in focus  \b0\par\par\uc2 736 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 13 Januar 2006\par 03:23\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 13 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fell on Friday, retreating from this week's multi-month peaks, as a narrowing in the U.S. trade deficit and the absence of a strong hawkish tone from the European \b \highlight22\uc2 Central Bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  bolstered the dollar.  \par \par \uc2  The South Korean won <KRW=><KRW=KFTC> led the decline in regionals, shedding more than 1 percent, with dealers citing hefty dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  after Finance Minister Han Duck-soo pledged a concerted effort to curb won strength.  \par \par \uc2  The won closed local trade at about 988 per dollar, after it had weakened from Thursday's highs near 974 -- its strongest since the Asian crisis in 1997.  \par \par \uc2  Indonesia added its voice to warnings in the region against sharp \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  gains. Indonesian Vice President Jusuf Kalla said on Friday steps needed to be taken to prevent the rupiah <IDR=> from getting too strong.  \par \par \uc2  Still, after a week marked by ups and downs in \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , analysts remained bullish on Asian regionals and viewed the U.S. dollar's recovery as short-lived.  \par \par \uc2  "We had the U.S. trade numbers yesterday and that caught everyone by surprise, so dollar/Asia moved higher. We've also had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  as well," said a trader in Hong Kong.  \par \par \uc2  "But people are still looking to sell dollar/Asia as there are those who weren't fast enough to get on to the trend. So the bias is still down for the dollar."  \par \par \uc2  The Indonesian rupiah was off an early peak of 9,335 per dollar, its highest in nearly 10 months. The Thai baht <THB=> slipped nearly 1 percent from Thursday's high near 39.28 a dollar, the strongest level since early April 2005.  \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE DOLLAR RETREATS  \par \par \uc2  Concerns that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  contained the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar <SGD=>, pushing it back from Thursday's 10-month highs near 1.6200.  \par \par \uc2  The Singapore dollar has gained about 3 percent in 3 weeks, which analysts say has driven it to near the top of its undisclosed band in a trade-weighted basket that the MAS uses to guide the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  Analysts said traders had been buying the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against the euro, yen and other \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  that they believe dominate the trade-weighted basket, and had now started booking profits.  \par \par \uc2  "Some people are buying the basket against the Sing dollar," Bhanu Baweja, UBS's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist, said. "I am not sure that is such a great idea. One should still be structurally long the Sing dollar."  \par \par \uc2  Other analysts said the recent gains in the Singapore dollar appeared overstretched.  \par \par \uc2  They said the potential for large merger and acquisition outflows, such as from a $6.2 billion bid Singapore state-owned port operator PSA has made for British ports and ferries firm P&O , could keep Sing dollar bulls at bay.  \par \par \uc2  "Some overshooting has taken place," said Jimmy Koh, head of economics and treasury at United Overseas Bank in Singapore. "The market is getting excited and this could be part of a new year phenomenon when hedge funds have a lot of money to invest."   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0827 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       114.53         114.06       -0.41\par  Sing dlr        1.6306         1.6237       -0.42\par  Taiwan dlr      31.985         31.874       -0.35\par  Korean won      987.30         973.80       -1.37\par  Baht             39.51          39.43       -0.20\par  Peso             52.38          52.35       -0.06\par  Rupiah         9340.00        9355.00       +0.16\par  Rupee            44.27          44.14       -0.28\par  Ringgit         3.7395         3.7405       +0.03\par  Yuan            8.0683         8.0659       -0.03\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       114.53         117.96       +2.99\par  Sing dlr        1.6306         1.6625       +1.96\par  Taiwan dlr      31.985         32.850       +2.70\par  Korean won      987.30        1011.60       +2.46\par  Baht             39.51          41.11       +4.05\par  Peso             52.38          53.09       +1.36\par  Rupiah         9340.00        9835.00       +5.30\par  Rupee            44.27          45.04       +1.75\par  Ringgit         3.7395         3.7790       +1.06\par  Yuan            8.0683         8.0702       +0.02\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2  (UPDATE 1)|LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|Z|IF|PHD|J|SNS|SNI|RNP|DNP|PTD  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060116e21d0003r\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
