\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Again Tests 10-Mo High Vs US Dollar Late  \b0\par\par\uc2 466 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2006\par 08:27\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose again to a near 10-month high Thursday, as market participants sold the U.S. dollar on concerns over major U.S. economic data due out later in the day.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond yields were higher in the long end than in the short end, resulting in curve steepening, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0645 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6223, down sharply from S$1.6375 in Asia Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 After opening near its intraday high of S$1.6298, the U.S. dollar fell to S$1.6214, its lowest since Mar. 17, 2005, as speculators and other players dumped the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  for the local dollar amid worries over the 1330 GMT release Thursday of U.S. trade deficit data for November.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said a wider-than-expected U.S. trade deficit could fuel the prevailing bearish sentiment toward the greenback and pave the way for the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fall further toward the six-year low of S$1.6161 set in March 2005 in coming sessions.  \par \par \uc2 In an apparent effort to temper the Singapore dollar's surge versus its U.S. counterpart Thursday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore was rumored to have bought a small amount of U.S. dollars around the S$1.6250 level in the morning, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 Given the Singapore dollar's recent strength, analysts such as DBS Bank's senior market strategist Philip Wee estimate that the trade-weighted Singapore dollar is very near to the upper limit of the band within which the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  manages the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The MAS operates a managed float regime for Singapore, which allows the trade-weighted exchange rate to fluctuate within an undisclosed policy band, and \b \highlight22\uc2 intervenes\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent it from breaching the band.  \par \par \uc2 In the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  government bond market, the yield on the 10-year bond rose more than that on the two-year bond, as Wednesday's rise in U.S. Treasury yields lifted the long end of the local yield curve more, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The following are the yields of Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps:  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                       Latest    Previous \par Overnight rate        3.3755%   3.0625% \par Two-year bond yield   2.77%     2.76% \par 10-year bond yield    3.33%     3.30% \par Two-year swap offer   3.37%     3.30% \par 10-year swap offer    3.65%     3.59% \par 2-10-yr swap spread:  28 BPS    29 BPs \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4159; ron.harui@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Michael Kitchen [ 12-01-06 0727GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020060112e21c0009d\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
