\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore dollar rises to 10-month high vs weak USD  \b0\par\par\uc2 316 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 Januar 2006\par 02:07\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Jan 12 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar extended its January gains to hit its highest levels in nearly 10 months on Thursday, buoyed by the U.S. dollar's broad weakness and the belief that Singapore authorities wanted a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  The Sing dollar <SGD=> rose overnight to levels around 1.6270/80 per U.S. dollar, its highest since March 2005, taking its gains in the past 3 weeks to nearly 3 percent.  \par \par \uc2  "The entire street seems to be short Sing dollar against the basket," said one local trader.  \par \par \uc2  He said the U.S. dollar's weakness, driven by the view that U.S. monetary tightening was close to an end, had pushed those bets against the Singapore dollar into the red and led to a short-covering.  \par \par \uc2  Besides, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS), the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 , had not \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to rein in the rallying Sing dollar as aggressively as other regional central banks, he said.  \par \par \uc2  "And with MAS \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  only in bits and pieces, it is making life for those Sing dollar shorts pretty miserable."  \par \par \uc2  The MAS's chief monetary policy tool is the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which it manages against an undisclosed trade-weighted band against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2  Analysts estimated the Sing dollar was now close to the top extremity of that band.  \par \par \uc2  Bhanu Baweja, UBS's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist, said in a note it was not advisable to be buying the Sing dollar against the U.S. dollar at these levels. But investors should try and be long the Sing dollar through options, he said.  \par \par \uc2  "This is based on our view that Singapore has stepped up the tightening of monetary policy as the economy has remained strong, and pressure on headline inflation is rising," Baweja said.     \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SINGAPORE-DOLLAR|LANGEN|SI|ABN|M|RBN|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060112e21c0002a\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw172\pich40\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2580\pichgoal600
