\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won down, baht steady, eyeing  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 529 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 10 Januar 2006\par 03:39\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 10 (Reuters) - The South Korean won and the Taiwan dollar slipped while other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  held steady on Tuesday in holiday-thinned trading as markets turned wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Markets in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Indonesia and Malaysia were closed for a Muslim festival holiday. That kept trading volumes thin.  \par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=> <KRW=KFTC> was quoted around 980 per dollar, just off Monday's high of 975, which was the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 's strongest level since the Asian financial crisis in 1997.  \par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso <PHP=> was barely changed at levels hugging 52.50 per dollar, just off Monday's peak of 52.25, which was its highest level since May 2003.  \par \par \uc2 "It's very tight trading. The dollar is up in other markets but not doing much against peso," said a Manila-based trader.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  slipped as the dollar staged a slight rebound from three-month lows struck the past couple of sessions against the euro <EUR=> and yen <JPY=>.  \par \par \uc2 Also, markets were taking a breather while watching how far central banks around the region would \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which have risen sharply since the start of the year.  \par \par \uc2 "With Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 FX\b0 \highlight\uc2  having rallied strongly already this year and central banks showing some, though not decisive, \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  appetite, a phase of consolidation today makes sense in this environment," Shahab Jalinoos, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist with ABN AMRO Bank said in a note.  \par \par \uc2 Markets should also be careful about selling the dollar against the Asians in such holiday trading for central banks could use the opportunity to push their \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  down, he said.  \par \par \uc2 "The key risk to long Asia positions today is that local central banks decide to take advantage of a modest USD bounce globally to ramp up \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and literally get more 'bang for their buck'," Jalinoos said.  \par \par \uc2 "While this will not reverse the longer term USD-Asia downtrend, it would make sense perhaps for them to try this if they are planning to engage only in a tactical as opposed to a strategic \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  policy." \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0226 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       114.45         114.20       -0.22\par  Taiwan dlr      32.015         31.942       -0.23\par  Korean won      980.30        0977.40       -0.30\par  Baht             39.82          39.78       -0.10\par  Peso             52.43          52.47       +0.08\par  Rupee            44.28          44.31       +0.07\par  Yuan            8.0664         8.0641       -0.03\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       114.45         117.96       +3.07\par  Sing dlr        1.6361         1.6625       +1.61\par  Taiwan dlr      32.015         32.850       +2.61\par  Korean won      980.30        1011.60     