\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Won, Taiwan dlr down,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  in focus  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Dhara Ranasinghe  \par \uc2 819 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Januar 2006\par 03:46\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Jan 6 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were mixed on Friday, with the South Korean won and Taiwan dollar down as regional authorities moved to cap \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength but the Malaysian ringgit and Thai baht extending recent gains.  \par \par \uc2 The won <KRW=><KRW=KTFC> eased as far as 996.9 per dollar after finance ministry and \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  officials held an emergency meeting after Thursday's sharp rise to about 985 per dollar, its highest level in more than eight years.  \par \par \uc2 South Korea would do its utmost to stabilise the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market, Vice Finance Minister Kwon Tae-shin said after the meeting on Friday morning.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers in Seoul said they spotted no dollar-buying \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  and the won, which has risen about 5 percent in the past month, had recovered some ground by late Asian trade.  \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> eased as much as 0.9 percent to 32.31 per U.S. dollar, with the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  seen \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a 4-1/2-month peak on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said that despite \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  would remain in demand, given expectations that U.S. monetary tightening may end and brighter economic data in Asia.  \par \par \uc2 "\b \highlight22\uc2 Intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  is unlikely to turn the tide in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ," said JPMorgan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Claudio Piron.  \par \par \uc2 "This is part of a broad dollar move that is also reflected in the equity markets. If data from Asia is strong, \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appreciation is justified and the best central banks can do is slow the level of that appreciation."  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> recovered from lows hit in early trade despite suspicion that the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was still checking levels.  \par \par \uc2 Traders suspected that \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  (MAS) had caused the Sing dollar to retreat from an overnight high of 1.6450 per U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 They had been expecting the MAS to \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  hit a seven-month high this week and moved near to the top end of its presumed trade-weighted band.  \par \par \uc2 RINGGIT, BAHT FIRM  \par \par \uc2 The Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> extended this week's rise to about 3.7505 per dollar -- its strongest level in 4-\u189\'00\'BD months.  \par \par \uc2 Investors have been encouraged by this week's relatively big move in the ringgit, which has traded in narrow ranges since its peg against the dollar was abandoned last July, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 They said the ringgit was bolstered by gains in Malaysia's stock market index <.KLSE>, which hit a two-month high on Friday, and expectations of foreign fund inflows this quarter.  \par \par \uc2 "People have got used to the fact that the ringgit doesn't move much. They have been shocked by the move this week and so there have been short-term players coming into the market," said Callum Henderson, Standard Chartered's head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy.  \par \par \uc2 The Thai baht <THB=> hit its strongest level in seven months at about 40.04 per dollar as the market tried to test a key chart barrier in the 40 baht per dollar area, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The focus turned to the U.S. non-farm payrolls report, due later on Friday. Analysts said the data would be the litmus test for whether the dollar could stage a rebound.  \par \par \uc2 "I am in the dollar-bear camp, but remember what happened at the start of last year when the dollar sold off then reversed?" said Henderson. "That's why there is a focus on the payrolls numbers. All we need is one strong number and everything could reverse the other way."   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 CURRENCIES\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  VS U.S. DOLLAR  Change on the day at 0806 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       116.12         115.86       -0.22\par  Sing dlr        1.6458         1.6443       -0.09\par  Taiwan dlr      32.190         32.016       -0.54\par  Korean won     0987.90        0987.30       -0.06\par  Baht             40.05          40.31       +0.65\par  Peso             52.50          52.59       +0.16\par  Rupiah         9573.00        9572.00       -0.01\par  Rupee            44.66          44.68       +0.04\par  Ringgit         3.7523         3.7575       +0.14\par  Yuan            8.0668         8.0675       +0.01\par  Change so far in 2006\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       116.12         117.96       +1.58\par  Sing dlr        1.6458         1.6625       +1.01\par  Taiwan dlr      32.190         32.850       +2.05\par  Korean won     0987.90        1011.60       +2.40\par  Baht      