\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Regional  \highlight22\uc2 currencies \highlight\uc2  rise to multi-month highs  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Dhara Ranasinghe  \par \uc2 868 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 4 Januar 2006\par 03:54\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Jan 4 (Reuters) - Asia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  markets enjoyed another day of stellar gains on Wednesday as the minutes from the last Federal Reserve meeting fuelled talk that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is almost done with lifting interest rates.  \par \par \uc2 Most regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , in a rally led by the Japanese yen <JPY=>, hit multi-month highs against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The South Korean <KRW=> <KRW=KFTC> strengthened past the psychologically important 1,000 mark to hit an 8-month high at 997.9 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> hit a 4-\u189\'00\'BD month peak at 1.6461 per dollar, the Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> set its highest level in almost a month at about 9,635 per dollar and the Taiwan dollar rose as much as one percent in local markets to hit a 4-month high of 32.33 per U.S. dollar.  \par \par \uc2 The minutes of the Fed's Dec. 13 meeting, released on Tuesday, showed the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's top officials believed the number of additional rate increases would not be large although its future action would depend on economic data.  \par \par \uc2 Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  had already started the new year on a strong footing, helped by a view that the U.S. monetary tightening that bolstered the dollar last year was unlikely to last much longer.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the minutes and data on Tuesday showing a drop in the U.S. Institute for Supply Management's factory index gave the rally in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  fresh momentum.  \par \par \uc2 "People are looking at what the big trade of this year will be and there are enough houses saying the dollar will have a poor year," said Westpac senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Sean Callow.  \par \par \uc2 "So people are either putting on new positions or receptive to news confirming their suspicions -- such as the ISM data."  \par \par \uc2 The sharp rise in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the spectre of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 A dealer in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said the market was wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar's sharp gains but had so far seen no signs of such action.  \par \par \uc2 South Korea's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was suspected of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market on Tuesday to cap the won's strength. A \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  official said on Wednesday that the won's latest rise was the result of an excessive reaction to the Fed minutes.  \par \par \uc2 "The market is unlikely to be afraid of the threat of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  from Korea," said Callow. "Korean authorities are aware that they are unlikely to stem the tide of a broad trend in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market."  \par \par \uc2 MORE THAN JUST A DOLLAR STORY  \par \par \uc2 The Philippine peso <PHP=> gained more than half a percent from Tuesday's close in local markets to a fresh 2-\u189\'00\'BD year peak of 52.37 per dollar, while the Thai baht <THB=> strengthened to 40.50 -- its strongest level against the dollar in 7 months.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said besides a soft tone in the U.S. dollar, investors were also responding to strong local equity markets, brighter economic data and favourable technical patterns.  \par \par \uc2 "There was strong (dollar) support in the 40.70/85 area and this has been broken," said a trader in Bangkok, referring to the baht. "We have also seen heavy offshore selling of dollar/baht this morning."  \par \par \uc2 The Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> rose and the yuan, traded in offshore derivative markets <CNYNDFOR=>, was pulled higher in line with the regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strength.  \par \par \uc2 Six-month non-deliverable forwards moved to price the yuan at 7.8675 per dollar, compared with 7.8730 late on Tuesday. The one-year contract priced the yuan at 7.7200 against the dollar from 7.7350 late the previous session.  \par \par \uc2 "The move in the NDFs is consistent with the move in the spot market and with the forecasts for a decline in the dollar in the months ahead," Callow said. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0818 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       115.95         117.12       +1.01\par  Sing dlr        1.6474         1.6566       +0.56\par  Taiwan dlr      32.330         32.645       +0.97\par  Korean won     0998.10        1005.50       +0.74\par  Baht             40.55          40.74       +0.47\par  Peso             52.41          52.66       +0.48\par  Rupiah         9660.00        9740.00       +0.83\par  Rupee            44.81          45.04       +0.53\par  Ringgit         3.7727         3.7782       +0.15\par  Yuan            8.0675         8.0709       +0.04\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       115.95         117.96       +1.73\par  Sing dlr        1.6474         1.6625       +0.92\par  Taiwan dlr      32.330         32.850       +1.61\par  K