\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore dollar highest in over 4 mths, data helps  \b0\par\par\uc2 346 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 3 Januar 2006\par 04:47\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2006 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2  SINGAPORE, Jan 3 (Reuters) - The Singapore dollar climbed on Tuesday to its highest level against the U.S. dollar in more than four months, boosted by data showing stronger-than-expected economic growth.  \par \par \uc2  Singapore's economy grew at an annualised rate of 9.7 percent in the fourth quarter of 2005, thanks to a big boost in manufacturing and stronger domestic demand, government data showed earlier. The figure was higher than a 7.2 percent growth rate forecast by economists in a Reuters poll last week.  \par \par \uc2  Together with a generally firm tone in Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , the data pushed the Singapore dollar <SGD=> to 1.6578 per U.S. dollar, its strongest level since mid-August.  \par \par \uc2  "The data continues to hint that there is a big chance that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore (MAS) will tighten policy at the April meeting and I think the market is reacting to that," said John Cairns, head of research at IDEAglobal in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2  "We've seen strong data throughout the fourth quarter and that raises the risk of tightening in April. It's not a sure thing but there may be some speculation on this."  \par \par \uc2  The MAS conducts monetary policy by guiding the trade-weighted Singapore dollar within an undisclosed band.  \par \par \uc2  Estimates on the width of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  band vary, but analysts and traders said the Singapore dollar was now trading in the strong side of the band.  \par \par \uc2  A trader said the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  could \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar moving too fast, too soon.  \par \par \uc2  "I think people are trying to test what levels the MAS will start to come in. According to our internal calculator, we are already testing the stronger side of the band -- a 1-\u189\'00\'BD   percent band on either side of the mid-point," he said.  \par \par \uc2  "If they do not come into the market, I think we should see further gains in the Sing dollar."     \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SINGAPORE-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 |LANGEN|Table|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020060103e2130003o\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
