quarter.  \par \par \uc2  Non-oil exports rose a higher-than-expected 14 percent to S$12.9 billion in November, the biggest annual rise in a year, government data showed on Friday.  \par \par \uc2  On a seasonally adjusted basis, non-oil exports fell a much smaller-than-expected 0.6 percent from October.  \par \par \uc2  "Singapore data are coming out pretty strong," said a dealer. "Everything is pointing to a stronger \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the near term."     \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-SINGAPORE-DOLLAR|LANGEN|ABN|M|RBN|SI|D|RNP|DNP|PTD|PMF  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051219e1cj0006h\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
