\par\par \b \uc2 DJ  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dlr Dn Late After Suspected  \highlight22\uc2 Forex Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 420 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 Dezember 2005\par 08:21\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was slightly weaker against the U.S. dollar in Asia late Friday after suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  on the \b \highlight22\uc2 foreign exchange\b0 \highlight\uc2  market.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond yields were mostly higher, mainly due to a rise in short-dated domestic interest rates, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0630 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6685, up from S$1.6676 late Thursday. It traded between S$1.6667 and S$1.6716 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 Early in the session, the U.S. dollar slipped to an intraday low of S$1.6667 due to its weakness versus the yen.  \par \par \uc2 But, the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  soon rose as high as S$1.6716 on rumored \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar from appreciating too much, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 'They apparently came in this morning,' a trader at a European bank said.  \par \par \uc2 MAS probably bought U.S. dollars around S$1.6685-S$1.6690, a \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dealer said.  \par \par \uc2 The MAS's suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market during \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  trading hours is unusual as it typically acts during European hours. The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  said it doesn't comment on its market \b \highlight22\uc2 operations\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 After the apparent \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the MAS, the U.S. gradually drifted back down to around S$1.6680 in extremely thin trade by late afternoon, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 On the Singapore government bond market, a rise in short-dated local interest rates pushed up yields across most of the curve, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The bid side for the domestic overnight interbank rate rose as high as 4.25%, its highest since October 1998, while the benchmark three-month Singapore interbank offered rate, or SIBOR, rose to 3.25%, its highest since Nov. 25, on strong borrowing interest from Singapore-based banks amid very thin liquidity, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The following are the yields of Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps:  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                       Latest   Previous \par Overnight rate        3.9375%  3.4659% \par Two-year bond yield   2.75%    2.74% \par 10-year bond yield    3.37%    3.35% \par Two-year swap offer   3.21%    3.19% \par 10-year swap offer    3.58%    3.58% \par 2-10-yr swap spread:  37 BPs   39 BPs \par   Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4159; ron.harui@dowjones.com -Edited by Genevieve Soledad -0-   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020051216e1cg005bp\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
