\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Rises To Fresh 3-Mo High Vs US Dlr Late  \b0\par\par\uc2 455 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 14 Dezember 2005\par 08:42\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose to a fresh three-month high in Asia late Wednesday, as players bought the local unit and other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the wake of Tuesday's meeting of the U.S. Federal Reserve's policy-making board.  \par \par \uc2 The yield curve of Singapore government bonds flattened slightly after the U.S. Federal Open Market Committee meeting, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0630 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6718, down from S$1.6757 late Tuesday. It traded between S$1.6693 and S$1.6743 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 From early in the session, U.S. funds sold the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  against its Asian counterparts, including the Singapore dollar, to take profit on long U.S. dollar positions versus those \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  after the Fed signaled that it is nearing an end to its monetary tightening cycle, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 As a result of the speculator-led selling of the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  versus the Singapore dollar, the U.S. dollar slipped to as low as S$1.6693 in the morning, its lowest since Aug. 24.  \par \par \uc2 Although the Fed raised interest rates by 25 basis points to 4.25%, as expected, the FOMC dropped its reference to monetary policy being accommodative, implying that U.S. interest rates are close to being neutral. The negative impact on the U.S. dollar was partially offset by the Fed's statement that it intends to hike rates at a "measured" pace.  \par \par \uc2 Later in the session, the U.S. dollar recovered to the S$1.6720 area on rumors that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb the sharp rise of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar versus the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 In the Singapore government bond market, short-dated yields edged up on the rise in short-term domestic interest rates. But long-term local bond yields fell in line with Tuesday's drop in U.S. Treasury's yields. This led to a very mild flattening of the curve, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 The following are the yields of Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps:  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                       Latest   Previous \par Overnight rate        3.0625%  2.5625% \par Two-year bond yield   2.70%    2.69% \par 10-year bond yield    3.33%    3.34% \par Two-year swap offer   3.17%    3.17% \par 10-year swap offer    3.60%    3.60% \par 2-10-yr swap spread:  43 BPs   43 BPs \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Ron Harui, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4159; ron.harui@dowjones.com [ 14-12-05 0742GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051214e1ce000at\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
