\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Broadly firm, rupiah in focus after rate move  \b0\par\par\uc2 By Dhara Ranasinghe  \par \uc2 821 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2005\par 03:26\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Dec 6 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were broadly firm against the dollar on Tuesday, boosted by gains in regional equities and optimism about economic growth in the region.  \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> hit a one-month peak at about 9,910 per dollar as investors cheered changes to the cabinet's top economic positions, but it dropped back slightly after Bank Indonesia delivered a smaller-than-expected interest rate rise.  \par \par \uc2 The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  raised the BI rate <BIPG>, its target rate for one-month certificates <BISBI01>, by 50 basis points to 12.75 percent to contain inflation, which is at a six-year high.  \par \par \uc2 This disappointed some in the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  market who had been looking for a rise of between 75 and 100 basis points.  \par \par \uc2 Still, analysts said sentiment was likely to stay upbeat after President Susilo Bambang Yudhoyono named respected former Finance Minister Boediono as his chief economics minister, replacing Aburizal Bakrie.  \par \par \uc2 Planning Minister Sri Mulyani Indrawati moves across to take on the finance portfolio from Jusuf Anwar.  \par \par \uc2 "Indonesia has been raising interest rates and hiring and firing the right people, so it is on the right track," said JPMorgan \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Claudio Piron. "The rupiah is likely to close up on the day but it will give up some of its gains."  \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won <KRW=><KRW=KTFC> gained more than a third of a percent to 1,033.0, boosted by foreign buying in the local equity market, whose index <.KS11> hit an all-time high.  \par \par \uc2 The Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP> added a quarter of a percent to a three-week high of 33.405 per dollar, helped by expectations that the victory of Taiwan's opposition party in local government elections at the weekend would spur more foreign fund inflows.  \par \par \uc2 Its success has been welcomed by financial markets because the opposition is viewed as having a more conciliatory approach to China, the island's top trading partner.  \par \par \uc2 GROWTH OPTIMISM  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said favourable economic data meant Asia's \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were holding up well against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "We are getting stronger-than-expected numbers for the third quarter and the export numbers are also showing that growth will be a bit better going into the first quarter despite high oil prices," said Jimmy Koh, head of economics and treasury at United Overseas Bank.  \par \par \uc2 Thailand's economy expanded 2.2 percent in the third quarter from the previous three months, beating market forecasts, data on Tuesday showed.  \par \par \uc2 Optimism about the economic outlook and rising short-term interest rates in Singapore helped push the Sing dollar <SGD=> to a two-month peak of about 1.6830 per dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Three-month rates <SGDF=> have risen to their highest level since early 2000. Traders said the upward pressure on rates was aimed at raising the appeal of local assets as interest rates around the region rise.  \par \par \uc2 "There is very strong macro data, a very strong push higher in domestic yields and a general recognition of the fact that the Sing dollar is cheaper against the basket," said Mirza Baig, a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Deutsche Bank in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Dealers in the Philippines said \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to cap the peso's strength had undermined the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  in early trade.  \par \par \uc2 The peso <PHP=> underperformed other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  for much of the day before strengthening slightly to about 53.87 per dollar in late trade.  \par \par \uc2 "We saw the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market this morning below the 54 level and that ruined the momentum, but we are stable now," said a trader in Manila. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR Change on the day at 0825 GMT   \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       121.04         121.28       +0.20\par  Sing dlr        1.6854         1.6889       +0.21\par  Taiwan dlr      33.458         33.493       +0.10\par  Korean won     1034.00        1036.50       +0.24\par  Baht             41.36          41.42       +0.15\par  Peso             53.87          53.98       +0.19\par  Rupiah         9925.00        9971.00       +0.46\par  Rupee            46.16          46.33       +0.36\par  Ringgit         3.7802         3.7803       +0.00\par  Yuan            8.0780         8.0808       +0.03\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       121.04         102.45      -15.36\par  Sing dlr        1.6854         1.6310       -3.23\par  Taiwan dlr      33.458         31.920       -4.60\par  Korean won     1034.00        1035.10       +0.11\par  Baht             41.36          38.88       -6.00\par  Peso             53.87          56.28       +4.47\par  Rupiah         9925.00        9290.00       -6.40\par  Rupee            46.16          43.47       -5.83\par  Ringgit         3.7802         3.8000       +0.52\par  Yuan            8.0780         8.2760       +2.45\par   \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKE