\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr At 7-Week High Late Tue, Bonds Fall On Tsys  \b0\par\par\uc2 431 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 6 Dezember 2005\par 09:26\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar extended its gains for a second consecutive session Tuesday to rise to a seven-week high as the yen recovered amid continued talk that China may allow the yuan to strengthen, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Government bonds fell amid thin trading volumes ahead of year-end holidays, reacting to overnight losses in U.S. Treasurys, they said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0738 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6846, down from S$1.6878 late Monday and below psychological support at S$1.6850. It traded between S$1.6840 and S$1.6875 intraday. The late Tuesday trade value of the Singapore dollar was its highest since Oct. 17, when the U.S. dollar traded at 1.6837.  \par \par \uc2 The local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  has been boosted by an economic rebound in the third quarter and signs that the last quarter will also remain healthy because of strong export demand for electronics and drugs from key U.S. and Asian markets.  \par \par \uc2 Tuesday's surge was helped partly by a slight recovery in the yen, which had fallen to a 32-month low against the U.S. dollar Monday, said a dealer at a local bank. The U.S. dollar was quoted at Y120.93 late Tuesday compared with Y121.23 in late Asian trade Monday.  \par \par \uc2 Larger gains in the Singapore unit were capped by fears that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2  to prevent a further appreciation in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , saidthe dealer.  \par \par \uc2 But a second dealer said the market may have overbought the Singapore dollar and that the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  appears poised for profit-taking Wednesday.  \par \par \uc2 United Overseas Bank said in a report said that the broad range for the U.S. dollar should be between S$1.6800 and S$1.7100 so long as the dollar is trading between Y120 and Y123.  \par \par \uc2 The following are the yields of Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps:  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                       Latest   Previous \par Overnight rate        2.313%   2.563% \par Two-year bond yield   2.68%    2.67% \par 10-year bond yield    3.29%    3.25% \par Two-year swap offer   3.18%    3.15% \par 10-year swap offer    3.55%    3.51% \par 2-10-yr swap spread:  37 BPs   36 BPs \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Ven Ram [ 06-12-05 0826GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051206e1c6000cm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
