\par\par \b \uc2 Weak Sing dlr,  \highlight22\uc2 intervention \highlight\uc2  push up  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  rates  \b0\par\par\uc2 574 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 17 November 2005\par 08:33\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2 , Nov 17 (Reuters) - Extended weakness in the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar and suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  to support it have pushed up short-term interest rates in Singapore to their highest in over four years, traders said on Thursday.  \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=> hit a 4-month low of 1.7065 against the U.S. dollar on Monday.  \par \par \uc2 It has recovered since, and was quoted around 1.7020/25 on Thursday, helped partly by \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  which some analysts suspect was to the tune of over U.S.$1 billion.  \par \par \uc2 But inter-bank rates have continued to climb higher. Three-month inter-bank rates <SGDF=> were quoted at 2.75/3.00 percent on Thursday, their highest levels since early 2001.  \par \par \uc2 The rate, which has been rising in the past 3 months, has jumped quite sharply from about 2.25 percent in early November.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts said one reason for the spike in yields has been a market belief that the Sing dollar will stay weak, despite the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2 's efforts to shore up the unit.  \par \par \uc2 "When people think that the exchange rate is not going to appreciate, they demand higher returns on money market deposits," said Deutsche Bank \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist Mirza Baig.  \par \par \uc2 "The \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  is preventing a further \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  depreciation, but if they want the Sing dollar to outperform the basket, they need to be much more aggressive."  \par \par \uc2 Unlike most central banks, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore's main policy tool is the trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 , which it manages in an undisclosed band.  \par \par \uc2 Analysts say the Sing dollar is in the weaker half of its policy band, although estimates on the width of the band vary.  \par \par \uc2 Bhanu Baweja, UBS's \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist, said interest rates and exchange rates in Singapore were closely linked.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore's markets adhered to uncovered-interest-parity theory, he said, which states that the expected movement in a \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pair equals the interest rate differential.  \par \par \uc2 "The Sing dollar remains weak and you need to be compensated for holding it through a higher interest rate," Baweja said.  \par \par \uc2 The MAS has had a tightening stance of allowing a "a modest and gradual appreciation" of the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  since April 2004.  \par \par \uc2 When it adopted that bias, the 3-month rate was about 0.44 percent, and the U.S. fed funds rate was 1.00 percent. The fed funds rate now stands at 4.00 percent and is expected to rise to 4.50 percent by the end of January next year.  \par \par \uc2 Other analysts said interest rates had also been driven up by banks covering a rising demand for consumer loans, especially mortgages.  \par \par \uc2 Moreover, by \b \highlight22\uc2 intervening\b0 \highlight\uc2  the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  was tightening the short-term supply of funds by selling U.S. dollars and soaking up Singapore dollars from the financial system, they said.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers added that the main focus for the Singapore dollar would remain the yen <JPY=>, which has weakened this week to 27-month lows against the dollar.  \par \par \uc2 "The key to dollar/Sing in the past few months has been dollar/yen," said Callum Henderson, head of \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy at Standard Chartered in Singapore.  \par \par \uc2 "There is still a very high correlation between the two because the yen is a key component of the trade-weighted basket and so if dollar/yen goes up, dollar/Sing goes up."  \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \highlight\uc2 -SINGAPORE|LANGEN|ABN|M|E|RBN|D|SI|RNP|DNP  \par \par \uc2 Dokument LBA0000020051117e1bh000qm\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
