rmaceutical exports.  \par \par \uc2 In the Singapore government bond market, the two-year bond yield rose to 2.71%, up three basis points, and the 10-year bond yield rose three basis points to 3.19%.  \par \par \uc2 The short end so far has led the selloff after the three-month Singapore interbank offered rate rose sharply in the last two weeks to close at 3% Monday, the highest in five years. On Tuesday, the three-month rate closed unchanged at 3%.  \par \par \uc2 The following are yields on Singapore government bonds and rates on interest-rate swaps.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                       Latest   Previous \par Overnight rate        2.69%    2.50% \par Two-year bond yield   2.71%    2.68% \par 10-year bond yield    3.19%    3.16% \par Two-year swap offer   3.07%    3.10% \par 10-year swap offer    3.50%    3.55% \par 2-10-yr swap spread:  43 BPs   45 BPs \par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site:  \f28 \par \par {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Paul Baylis [ 15-11-05 0743GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020051115e1bf000e0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
