\par\par \b  \highlight22\uc2 Singapore \highlight\uc2  Dollar Steady Late; Mkt Fears MAS  \highlight22\uc2 Intervention \highlight\b0\par\par\uc2 341 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 September 2005\par 09:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 SINGAPORE\b0 \highlight\uc2  (Dow Jones)--The \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was little changed in late Asian trade Friday as fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  prevented the local unit from breaking a key support, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Government bond prices were flat at the long end and rose at the short end, which slightly steepened the yield curve.  \par \par \uc2 At 0655 GMT, the U.S. dollar was at S$1.6897 compared with S$1.6895 Thursday. It traded between S$1.6882 and S$1.6915 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 A dealer at a local bank said the U.S. dollar ended below psychological resistance of S$1.6900 because of fears of \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  ahead of the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 's policy review.  \par \par \uc2 Most participants expect the MAS' strong stance at its semiannual monetary policy review in middle of October will give the Singapore dollar a psychological boost.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the U.S. dollar's drop against the euro also helped the Singapore dollar as the European single \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is 15% of Singapore's trade-weighted basket.  \par \par \uc2 In the short term U.S. dollar faces stiff resistance at S$1.6920 and support at S$1.6870, which should keep it in a range, said Oversea-Chinese Banking Corp. in a report.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore targets the exchange rate, rather than interest rates, as its monetary policy tool since its exports and imports amount to three times the city-state's S$184 billion economy.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest     Previous \par    Overnight rate       2.44%      2.25% \par    Two-year bond yield  2.30%      2.33% \par    10-year bond yield   2.86%      2.86% \par    Two-year swap offer  2.47%      2.48% \par    10-year swap offer   3.16%      3.15% \par    2-10-yr swap spread  69 BPs     67 BPs \par  \par    Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par  \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Mary de Wet [ 30-09-05 0756GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050930e19u000a0\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
