ose to 2.41%, compared with 2.20% as investors were bearish because of upcoming supply of corporate and government bonds.  \par \par \uc2 In an auction Wednesday, the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore sold S$1.1 billion of five-year government bonds at a cutoff yield of 2.65%. Settlement is due Oct. 3.  \par \par \uc2 Traders said the Housing Development Board is expected to price its S$500 million of bonds soon, and that will add to bearish sentiment in the middle and short end of the curve.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest     Previous \par    Overnight rate       2.20%      2.29% \par    Two-year bond yield  2.41%      2.33% \par    10-year bond yield   2.95%      2.95% \par    Two-year swap offer  2.51%      2.48% \par    10-year swap offer   3.22%      3.24% \par    2-10-yr swap spread  71 BPs     76 BPs \par  \par    Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par  \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Paul Baylis [ 28-09-05 0825GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050928e19s000ds\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
