\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Singapore Dollar Down Late On Weak Euro  \b0\par\par\uc2 352 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 19 September 2005\par 09:56\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar fell in late Asian trade Monday, hurt by the euro's weakness after unconvincing election results in Germany, Europe's biggest economy.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bond prices fell, tracking overnight losses in U.S. Treasurys, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0654 GMT, the U.S. unit was S$1.6833, up from S$1.6782 Friday. It traded between S$1.6810 and S$1.6840.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the Singapore dollar opened weaker after the euro tumbled to a one-month low against the U.S. dollar in early trade.  \par \par \uc2 The common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  was hurt after conservative challenger Angela Merkel's party won most votes in German elections Sunday but fell short of a clear mandate to govern against incumbent Gerhard Schroeder.  \par \par \uc2 The euro fell to as low as $1.2132 as of 0518 GMT, its lowest since Aug. 19. Any weakness in the euro hurts the Singapore dollar as the common \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is about 15% of Singapore's trade-weighted \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  basket, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 A dealer at a Singapore bank said despite early weakness, the local unit remained stuck in a narrow range because of strong support at S$1.6850.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said the market was wary of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  because the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar was trading on the weaker side of its trade-weighted band.  \par \par \uc2 JPMorgan in a report said the Singapore dollar's current weakness is at odds with strong economic data last week, including faster-than-expected growth in non-oil exports and retail sales.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                         Latest     Previous \par    Overnight rate       2.063%     2.125% \par    Two-year bond yield  2.21%      2.20% \par    10-year bond yield   2.95%      2.94% \par    Two-year swap offer  2.38%      2.36% \par    10-year swap offer   3.20%      3.14% \par    2-10-yr swap spread  82 BPs     78 BPs \par    Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed on the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com -Edited by Genevieve Soledad -0-   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050919e19j004jx\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
