\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dollar Lower Late; Pares Losses On MAS Fears  \b0\par\par\uc2 463 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 15 September 2005\par 10:46\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar was lower in late Asian trade Thursday as broad gains in the U.S. dollar hurt most Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 The local unit recovered from early lows on fears the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  may \b \highlight22\uc2 intervene\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  government bond prices fell, tracking overnight selling in U.S. Treasurys, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0701 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6801, up from S$1.6790 Wednesday. It traded between S$1.6781 and S$1.6812 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 In the morning session, the U.S. dollar rose to S$1.6812, following the greenback's rise against the yen and the euro, said a dealer at a Singapore bank.  \par \par \uc2 However fears that the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of Singapore may prevent larger weakness in the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  prevented players from taking the dollar further higher, he said.  \par \par \uc2 Speculation that Singapore's state-owned investment company, Temasek Holdings, may be in the market to buy foreign \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to fund recent acquisition of stakes in Chinese banks has also kept the Singapore dollar under downward pressure, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 However most analysts have recently made calls for the Singapore dollar to strengthen because MAS is likely to continue with its current policy of modest and gradual appreciation of the exchange rate adopted in April 2004.  \par \par \uc2 DBS Bank in its \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategy said the Singapore dollar should rebound from the weak limit of its trade-weighted band toward the stronger half as the MAS is unlikely to change policy in its next review in October.  \par \par \uc2 It recommends buying the Singapore dollar against a basket of \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  comprising the U.S. dollar, euro and Japanese yen.  \par \par \uc2 Sabrina Jacobs, \b \highlight22\uc2 forex\b0 \highlight\uc2  strategist at Dresdner Kleinwork Wasserstein, said the upside for the U.S. dollar against the Singapore dollar is likely to be capped at S$1.6830 because of tight MAS policy.  \par \par \uc2 She said the U.S. dollar may have strongly rebounded recently, but a firm outlook on the greenback would likely depend on a spate of economic data due this week.  \par \par \uc2 Key would be the consumer price index, which may determine the outlook for the Federal Reserve's current tightening stance.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest     Previous \par    Overnight rate       2.000%    2.0625% \par    Two-year bond yield  2.17%      2.14% \par    10-year bond yield   2.92%      2.88% \par    Two-year swap offer  2.38%      2.34% \par    10-year swap offer   3.16%      3.14% \par    2-10-yr swap spread: 78 BPs     80 BPs \par  \par    Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par  \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhar@dowjones.com  \f28 \par \par \uc2 \f2 -Edited by Gauri Bhatia [ 15-09-05 0846GMT ]  \f28 \par \par \uc2 1163 1859  \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJI0000020050915e19f000e5\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
