\par\par \b \uc2 DJ Singapore Dollar Up Late On Yen's Early Poll-Linked Gains  \b0\par\par\uc2 482 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 12 September 2005\par 09:30\par \uc2 Dow Jones Chinese Financial Wire\par \uc2 DJCFWE\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 Copyright (c) 2005, Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar rose in late Asian trade Monday, reacting to the yen's early gains after a landslide election victory for Japan's ruling coalition.  \par \par \uc2 Government bonds fell at the short end as the overnight rate rose, and was little changed at the long end, which helped steepen the yield curve, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0624 GMT, the U.S. dollar was S$1.6747, down from S$1.6779 late Friday. It traded between S$1.6725 and S$1.6751 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 The election victory of Japanese Prime Minister Junichiro Koizumi's Liberal Democratic Party and its coalition partner, New Komeito Party, pushed the U.S. dollar to Y108.96 in early trade, the yen's strongest level since Sept. 5.  \par \par \uc2 Later, the U.S. dollar recovered ground and was little changed from its New York close of Y109.61 as selling by Japanese importers offset the wave of election-related yen-buying.  \par \par \uc2 The brief yen rally provided support for the \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar, which had already stabilized from suspected \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  late Friday, traders said.  \par \par \uc2 Amy Yeo, treasury economist at United Overseas Bank, said the Singapore dollar was poised for more gains if the yen rallies further.  \par \par \uc2 Another important factor would be if Japan's Nikkei 225 Stock Average climbs above 13,000 points, which would be a psychological boost for the yen and Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 , she said. Monday, the Nikkei 225 closed up 204.39 points at 12896.43.  \par \par \uc2 'This would trigger yen longs and would further weaken the dollar-Sing (U.S. dollar against the Singapore dollar), she said.  \par \par \uc2 Other traders were cautious over the outlook for the local \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Oversea-Chinese Banking Corp. said in a note that it saw strong support for the U.S. dollar at S$1.6700, while saying it would rather wait for U.S. trade data Tuesday before forming a short-term outlook for the Singapore dollar.  \par \par \uc2 On the money market, the overnight rate rose to 2% from 1.9250% Friday, pushing the two-year yield up two basis points to 2.07%.  \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they suspected the MAS may be behind the higher overnight rate since last week as it was trying to squeeze liquidity to curb speculative selling of the Singapore dollar.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par                         Latest     Previous \par    Overnight rate       2.00%      1.9250% \par    Two-year bond yield  2.07%      2.05% \par    10-year bond yield   2.84%      2.84% \par    Two-year swap offer  2.28%      2.25% \par    10-year swap offer   3.08%      3.10% \par    2-10-yr swap spread: 80 BPs     85 BPs \par    Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \par \uc2 \f2 -By Saeed Azhar, Dow Jones Newswires; 65-6415-4157; saeed.azhari@dowjones.com -0-   \f28 \par \par \uc2 Dokument DJCFWE0020050912e19c004ed\par }\page {\par\fs20{\*\shppict{\pict\pngblip\picw184\pich22\picscaley100\picscalex100\picwgoal2760\pichgoal330
