\par\par \b \uc2 Singapore Dlr Falls To 5-Week Low Vs US Dlr Late  \b0\par\par\uc2 549 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 30 August 2005\par 09:12\par \uc2 Dow Jones International News\par \uc2 DJI\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Dow Jones & Company, Inc.  \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE (Dow Jones)--The Singapore dollar fell to a five-week low against its U.S. counterpart in late Asian trade Tuesday, dragged down by receding worries over the impact of high oil prices on the U.S. economy and by weakness in regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .  \par \par \uc2 Singapore government bonds were weaker across the board following a disappointing auction of 15-year bonds Monday, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 At 0642 GMT, the U.S. unit was at S$1.6833, up from S$1.6753 late Monday. It traded between S$1.6782 and S$1.6849 intraday.  \par \par \uc2 The U.S. dollar kicked off Tuesday's Asian session on a positive note against the local dollar, bolstered by diminishing concerns over the adverse effects of higher oil prices on the U.S. economy and by the pronounced weakness of the yen and the Indonesian rupiah.  \par \par \uc2 Singapore-based interbank players eventually boosted the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  to S$1.6849, its highest level since July 21.  \par \par \uc2 Tuesday, the U.S. unit soared as high as Y111.09. At 0642 GMT, it was quoted at Y111.00, up from Y110.61 in New York late Monday.  \par \par \uc2 The rupiah, meanwhile, continued tumbling Tuesday, with the U.S. dollar rising above IDR11,000, marking the lowest level for the rupiah since July 2001.  \par \par \uc2 Given lingering concerns over high oil prices, sentiment toward Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  such as the Singapore dollar remained negative, analysts said.  \par \par \uc2 But traders said wariness over possible \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  by the \b \highlight22\uc2 Monetary Authority\b0 \highlight\uc2  of \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  to curb excessive depreciation of the Singapore dollar could slow the current rally of the U.S. dollar versus its Singaporean counterpart in coming sessions.  \par \par \uc2 "Caution about \b \highlight22\uc2 intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  may emerge should (the U.S. dollar-\b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  dollar) rally too quickly," OCBC Bank said in a research report.  \par \par \uc2 From a technical analysis perspective, the S$1.6870-S$1.6880 area is a strong resistance region and a clear U.S. dollar rise above there seems unlikely for the global session, United Overseas Bank said in a research report.  \par \par \uc2 Having said that, however, UOB also said only a U.S. dollar pullback below the S$1.6770 support level would suggest that the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  is entering a consolidation phase against the Singapore dollar.  \par \par \uc2 Yields on Singapore government bonds rose along the curve, mainly due to Monday's weaker-than-expected auction of S$2.7 billion worth of 15-year bonds, dealers said.  \par \par \uc2 With a cutoff yield of 3.30% and an average yield of 3.18%, the so-called "tail" of the auction was 12 basis points, which was considered overly long and was indicative of weak investor demand, dealers added.  \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  \par                         Latest     Previous \par    Overnight rate       1.9375%    1.8750% \par    Two-year bond yield  2.07%      2.04% \par    10-year bond yield   2.86%      2.84% \par    Two-year swap offer  2.28%      2.25% \par    10-year swap offer   3.10%      3.08% \par    2-10-yr swap spread: 82 BPs     83 BPs \par  \par    Historical bond yields and final prices can be viewed at the \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Monetary Authority\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2  of Singapore's bond Web site: \par  \par     \f28 {\field{\*\fldinst{HYPERLINK "http://www.sgs.gov.sg"}}{\fldrslt{\cf2 \uc2 http://www.sgs.gov.sg }}}\par \p