\par\par \b \uc2 Emerging Asia  \highlight22\uc2 FX \highlight\uc2 -Weaker but yen rally helps curb losses   \b0\par\par\uc2 759 \uc2 W\u246\'00\'F6rter\par \uc2 16 August 2005\par 05:11\par \uc2 Reuters News\par \uc2 LBA\par \uc2 Englisch\par \uc2 (c) 2005 Reuters Limited   \par \par \uc2 SINGAPORE, Aug 16 (Reuters) - Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  were weaker on Tuesday, weighed down by worries about the impact of high oil prices on economic growth, but trimmed some of their losses as the yen hit a seven-week high against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The Indonesian rupiah <IDR=> extended Monday's falls to hit its lowest level since March 2002 at about 9,920 per dollar.   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said they suspected the \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  had \b \highlight22\uc2 intervened\b0 \highlight\uc2  in the market to support the rupiah, helping the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  pull away from its lows.   \par \par \uc2 The South Korean won <KRW=><KRW=KFTC> and Malaysian ringgit <MYR=> underperformed most other Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 The ringgit eased more than a third of a percent to 3.767 per dollar. Analysts said offshore speculators were selling the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  on expectations that the ringgit was unlikely to strengthen as much as anticipated against the dollar near term.   \par \par \uc2 The Singapore dollar <SGD=>, which hit a two-week low against the U.S. \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  overnight, and the Taiwan dollar <TWD=TP>, which slipped to a one-month low earlier, pared their falls.   \par \par \uc2 "The sell-off has been fairly contained, although the rupiah is the one that looks dicey given the break out of its recent range," said BNP Paribas senior \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  analyst Thio Chin Loo.   \par \par \uc2 "The yen is a factor that is helping mitigate losses, so by and large Asian \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2  haven't been suffering too much despite the rebound in the dollar against European \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 ."   \par \par \uc2 The yen <JPY=> hit a seven-week peak against the dollar on growing optimism about Japan's economy.   \par \par \uc2 One Singapore-based dealer said equity flows out of Asia, excluding Japan, into the world's second-largest economy were helping the yen outperform other regional \b \highlight22\uc2 currencies\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Analysts at UBS said in a note that a decrease in the market's appetite for risk had meant that a strong run of portfolio inflows into Asia, excluding Japan, was now moderating.   \par \par \uc2 "However, this is a bigger worry for economies in Southeast Asia, where declining terms of trade and higher import volumes have also meant a sharp contraction in current account surpluses," the note said.   \par \par \uc2 RUPIAH WOES   \par \par \uc2 Analysts said the technical outlook for the rupiah was bleak after the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2  broke through key chart support in the 9,900 per dollar area.   \par \par \uc2 "The next test will be the 10,000 psychological level and if that breaks, I would see little resistance for dollar/rupiah until 10,220," said Wayne Wong, a technical analyst at IDEAglobal in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Dealers said suspicions of \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank intervention\b0 \highlight\uc2  limited selling in the rupiah. A trader in \b \highlight22\uc2 Singapore\b0 \highlight\uc2  said comments from Bank Indonesia also supported the \b \highlight22\uc2 currency\b0 \highlight\uc2 .   \par \par \uc2 Indonesia's \b \highlight22\uc2 central bank\b0 \highlight\uc2  governor said on Tuesday a government target of 9,400 rupiah per dollar in 2006 was realistic.   \par \par \uc2 The rupiah has lost more than six percent of its value since the start of the year, due mainly to rising inflation and soaring oil prices, which have increased the dollar buying of state oil company Pertamina to finance oil imports.   \par \par \uc2 Pertamina has bought a total of about 18.23 million barrels of oil products for September, its highest monthly volume of imports this year and 15 percent more than in August, industry sources said on Tuesday. \b \highlight22\uc2 CURRENCIES\b0 \highlight\uc2  VS U.S. DOLLAR    \par \par \uc2 \f2 \par  Change on the day at   0820 GMT\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid   Previous day    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       109.07         109.50       +0.39\par  Sing dlr        1.6575         1.6540       -0.21\par  Taiwan dlr      31.989         31.966       -0.07\par  Korean won     1016.30        1013.80       -0.25\par  Baht             41.06          40.98       -0.19\par  Peso             55.69          55.77       +0.14\par  Rupiah         9900.00        9887.00       -0.13\par  Rupee            43.53          43.53       +0.00\par  Ringgit         3.7655         3.7530       -0.33\par  Yuan            8.1002         8.0976       -0.03\par  Change on year\par  \f28 \b \highlight22\uc2 \f2 Currency\f28 \b0 \highlight\uc2 \f2     Latest bid  End prev year    Pct Move\par  Japan yen       109.07         102.45       -6.07\par  Sing dlr        1.6575         1.6310       -1.60\par  Taiwan dlr      31.989         31.920       -0.22\par  Korean won     1016.30        1035.10       +1.85\par  Baht             41.06          38.88       -5.31\par  Peso             55.69          56.28       +1.06\par  Rupiah         9900.00        9290.00       -6.16\par  Rupee            43.53          43.47       -0.14\par  Ringgit         3.7655         3.8000       +0.92\par  Yuan            8.1002         8.2760       +2.17\par    \f28 \par \par \uc2 MARKETS-ASIA-\b \highlight22\uc2 FOREX\b0 \hi